SEEKWR - writes past the end, and the write of nothing
--- on the kernel
4 bytes at 100000 in an empty file: ok
  100004 long: ok
  read back from 100000: ok
nothing written at 300000, 300000 long: ok
  its clusters taken from the free count: ok
4 bytes at 250000, read back: ok
  the ones at 100000 still there: ok
nothing written at 50000, 50000 long: ok
  the clusters past it given back: ok
closed and opened again, still 50000 long: ok
deleted, every cluster back: ok
parking the kernel, to make them there too...
